Subject: [PATCH] compose: the claimed OS picks the GPU, even with no host GPU

The claimed platform selects the GPU identity, and the host's graphics
driver plays no part in the choice. A macOS or Windows host defaults to
a profile of its own platform, and a Linux host defaults to a Windows
profile, the usual deployment. A host with no GPU gets a hardware
renderer string drawn by seed from the claimed platform's measured GPUs,
never the one SwiftShader string every such host would share. The
SwiftShader identity is served only when --fingerprint-anchor names it,
and --fingerprint-platform=linux overrides the Linux default.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -57,6 +57,13 @@
